<%# Connect, step 1: what connecting a contract to your own organization
    does. From the controller: @contract, @organizations (the ones they
    run), @shows (the contract's dates). %>
<% content_for :title, "Connect your contract" %>
<%
  org = @contract.organization.name
  show_name = (@contract.production&.name || @contract.production_name).to_s
  contractor = @contract.contractor_name.presence || "you"
  coming = @shows.reject(&:canceled)
  mine = @organizations.one? ? @organizations.first.name : "your organization"
  none_yet = @organizations.empty?
%>
<div class="w-full mb-10">
  <%= render "my/contract_connections/steps", step: 1 %>

  <div class="bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 shadow-sm p-4 sm:p-8">

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2 coustard-regular"><%= none_yet ? "See your #{org} dates in an organization of your own" : "Connect your #{org} contract to #{mine}" %></h2>
  <%# Said by who the contract is with and what it's for: the show, the
      contractor and their organization often share one name, so "X is your
      show, and you run it in X" told nobody anything (Tim, 2026-11-17).
      The words are Tim's (2026-11-18): what the contract presents, not how
      many dates, and what connecting links. %>
  <p class="text-gray-600 mt-2">
    <%= org %> has a contract with <%= contractor %><%= " to present #{show_name}" if show_name.present? && !show_name.casecmp?(contractor) %>.
    <% if none_yet %>
      If you run this show yourself on CocoScout, in an organization of your own, you can connect it to <%= possessive(org) %> contract.
      The dates, ticket sales, and mailing lists are then linked, and your team is able to see much more information.
    <% else %>
      You also run <%= @organizations.one? ? "an organization of your own on CocoScout, #{@organizations.first.name}" : "organizations of your own on CocoScout" %>.
      When you connect <%= @organizations.one? ? "your organization" : "one of them" %> to <%= possessive(org) %> contract, the dates, ticket sales, and mailing lists
      are linked, and your team is able to see much more information.
    <% end %>
  </p>

  <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-6">
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
      <%= render "shared/section_heading", padding: "px-4 py-3", title: "What you'll get from #{org}" %>
      <ul class="p-4 space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-600">
        <li><span class="block font-medium text-gray-900">Their dates appear in your show's calendar.</span>
          You won't need to enter them yourself. If <%= org %> moves or cancels a date, yours changes to match, and you'll be asked to let your cast know.</li>
        <li><span class="block font-medium text-gray-900">You'll see how each date is selling.</span>
          Everyone who manages <%= mine %> can see the ticket sales, not only you.</li>
        <li><span class="block font-medium text-gray-900">Your team and cast can follow along too.</span>
          You decide whether they can see how many tickets have sold.</li>
        <li><span class="block font-medium text-gray-900">The people who follow your shows come with it.</span>
          If <%= org %> keeps a mailing list for your shows, the people on it appear in your own organization's Mailing lists.</li>
        <li><span class="block font-medium text-gray-900">The ticket page can show your own art.</span>
          <%= possessive(org) %> ticket page for these dates will use the poster, wide image, and description from your production, unless <%= org %> chooses to keep its own.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
      <%= render "shared/section_heading", padding: "px-4 py-3", title: "What stays the same" %>
      <ul class="p-4 space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-600">
        <li><span class="block font-medium text-gray-900">Your contract and what it pays don't change.</span>
          Connecting adds nothing to the contract, and you can unlink whenever you like.</li>
        <li><span class="block font-medium text-gray-900">Your side of the show stays private.</span>
          Your messages with your performers and what you pay people are never shared with <%= org %>.</li>
        <li><span class="block font-medium text-gray-900"><%= org %> still runs the box office.</span>
          Prices, ticket types, the door, comps, and settling each date remain theirs.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <% if none_yet %>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-4">You'll need an organization of your own first. Creating one is free, and when it's ready you can come back to My Contracts and connect this contract to it.</p>
  <% elsif @standing_organization %>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-4"><%= org %> has already agreed to connect your later contracts to <%= @standing_organization.name %>, so this one won't need their approval again. It will connect as soon as you finish these steps, and <%= org %> will be notified.</p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-4"><%= org %> needs to accept before anything happens. Until they do, nothing changes for either of you.</p>
  <% end %>

  <div class="mt-8 flex items-center justify-between">
    <% if @contract.connect_offer_dismissed_at.nil? %>
      <%= form_with url: my_contract_connection_not_now_path(@contract), method: :patch, local: true do %>
        <%= render "shared/button", text: "Not now", variant: "secondary", size: "medium", type: :submit %>
      <% end %>
    <% else %>
      <%= render "shared/button", text: "Back", variant: "secondary", size: "medium", path: my_contracts_path %>
    <% end %>
    <% if none_yet %>
      <%= render "shared/button", text: "Create your organization", variant: "primary", size: "medium", path: new_manage_organization_path %>
    <% else %>
      <%= render "shared/button", text: "Continue", variant: "primary", size: "medium",
            path: my_connect_contract_production_path(@contract) %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  </div>
</div>
